{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1786658646004708001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"albinic-agrologic-dolphin","assignee":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","attestations":{"plan-review":{"algorithm":"sshsig","author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","envelope":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.opcert.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","head_sha":"2af5a4c773925336d38697b1bb681a6fd70ce9cd","key_id":null,"kind":"plan-review","manifest":["plan-review: PASS","ticket: 0078-fa3e-05d1-4e12","material: 07f5bddf9845d356","material-part: children 647ea2107ca5072f 0","material-part: description 64924973fbeb3bd0 6551","material-part: description_boxes 399141be1d30ac26 0","material-part: file_impact 013a92f5f2f04d9a 1","material-part: ticket_id ad17e222cd09eefd 19","model: bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","runner: pydantic_ai","blocking: 0","advisory: 1","review-phase: planning","rebar-version: 0.11.0 (2af5a4c773)","regver: 4f90349cd81c4911","verified-at-sha:c389e4c8b9c0cdad8ae44e6091bed6f566e43dd4","dep a2d4e72a15b8247f783ede72ad979a36a84a1e65fec64629df05806c3f9a01fe tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py","read-set: 2","read-path: tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_corpus.py","read-path: tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py","currency-basis: file_impact"],"material_fingerprint":"07f5bddf9845d356","merged_log_commit":"c389e4c8b9c0cdad8ae44e6091bed6f566e43dd4","principal":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","signature":null,"signed_at":1786651714130371000}},"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":11,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"fe47c8d0c3733352a2d04ece5e267b0486fce18b47c9586a26714670a9c4218f","event_uuid":"fef84a97-f915-4a10-a662-de95875f99e2","position":{"commit_sha":"ef5b43e5abda64898bc95ab62273297f55a7742d","position":"1786650105971258001-fef84a97-f915-4a10-a662-de95875f99e2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"0bc6ba023bff964c1295eb5d664177db4c439dd2e9c76b77d90af6dd550883d7","event_uuid":"37adfab1-bb91-43f3-a63b-1053c66e888c","position":{"commit_sha":"528b58b991d47b95f64003a233041442aad24446","position":"1786650131515107001-37adfab1-bb91-43f3-a63b-1053c66e888c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e954f3b7766ee8173beeb95d95edde207bed9c8c4faddae1d0746abcccba15db","event_uuid":"b94ccc31-1072-4789-8064-97d50f34db60","position":{"commit_sha":"c8b49969e6a24bdb0bed63a214d20c4b5fcf88ea","position":"1786651475905843001-b94ccc31-1072-4789-8064-97d50f34db60"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6bacce5a59b82aae00b529b678ce602bfc28ab9e06b5729ab1e184b180319922","event_uuid":"3de60824-cb2f-4ce7-9f48-2ef4805ac88d","position":{"commit_sha":"ad110b87827fde79ccdd1fb46ae1fe4018aba2d4","position":"1786651483478927001-3de60824-cb2f-4ce7-9f48-2ef4805ac88d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e8806ee1d9e94df5702a0fdf591d93dbebbe5f33a43bf09cb381c7c74a671245","event_uuid":"95299c36-e67c-4d0f-a7de-729b60af90a7","position":{"commit_sha":"346329121c8b6feec7ad21ae974cb691af541be1","position":"1786651714134722001-95299c36-e67c-4d0f-a7de-729b60af90a7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f7171ad6e550abcb60d1c3c32386d80348a2fb5fc4a7c4e51d9fcc0b1cda24d9","event_uuid":"941ca602-df75-495d-858a-6a65ba03112e","position":{"commit_sha":"9a02f6664c8111e0e39667a5a9e8417ecdc63913","position":"1786651730308690001-941ca602-df75-495d-858a-6a65ba03112e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ec1d99e796ec0c8a540fb3aab577021ff1c38ea866de5e162360790314400bed","event_uuid":"31d34671-f71f-4246-8658-de659cd62d33","position":{"commit_sha":"9a02f6664c8111e0e39667a5a9e8417ecdc63913","position":"1786651731925824001-31d34671-f71f-4246-8658-de659cd62d33"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"4616f896c1dccc80b25289693d2c8df154fa58f7d15af89386bdc3aa38207cd8","event_uuid":"6da15436-97de-4dec-a707-95d1251fbd71","position":{"commit_sha":"411c0bd2c4fc6984f59d027a0fe48f5f3787c734","position":"1786652175008917001-6da15436-97de-4dec-a707-95d1251fbd71"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"5280077d06f423a38a04b0a815c2df76eb9c542e6116cb34494199c65ad7ba92","event_uuid":"8c2230eb-da6f-4369-aa15-3d51b015a7d3","position":{"commit_sha":"e29ab37db5a10cc80bdda7b455a4e678557d9606","position":"1786653629163683001-8c2230eb-da6f-4369-aa15-3d51b015a7d3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"67e6a086487988cc573e1ac1419d373ba400e122a351bf8218fbe1fb436cd8ce","event_uuid":"219dd0ac-cb08-49cf-b85d-79c6052b154b","position":{"commit_sha":"ed8184d0570102d5854f810c609855b295f48a26","position":"1786655574860398001-219dd0ac-cb08-49cf-b85d-79c6052b154b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"3106d2b335d15087c1eac1a64c5cae172a3174de020cd5cce2b8425b64f67cd9","event_uuid":"a3c7d5e9-cb8f-42ec-87a0-68f0b8dd8a3c","position":{"commit_sha":"157dd5c65f0a7c3b002879b5e9267d76b5349152","position":"1786655694699609653-a3c7d5e9-cb8f-42ec-87a0-68f0b8dd8a3c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-227_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"SECOND OCCURRENCE — same test, same cell, different run. Strengthens the reproduction evidence materially.\n\nRun 31737094701 (change 1731, patchset 2, after a recheck of run 31734135055 on the IDENTICAL tree):\n- macos-latest/py3.13 only; the three ubuntu cells passed both times.\n- 1 failed, 12849 passed, 65 skipped, in 1602.64s (first occurrence: 1664.64s).\n- Same test: tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py::test_rendered_output_is_byte_identical_to_the_landed_renderer.\n\nNEW TIMING DETAIL, which I think is the most useful thing here for reproduction: the two log events are 14 minutes apart.\n  19:57:28  .....[gw1] node down: Not properly terminated\n  20:11:28  worker 'gw1' crashed while running <the test>\nThe worker is declared down at 19:57:28 and the crash is only attributed at 20:11:28. That gap is consistent with a HANG followed by a kill, not with a fast crash — which fits the 300s-per-test-timeout hypothesis in the ticket body, but note 14 minutes is far longer than 300s, so if the per-test timeout were firing cleanly the gap should be ~5 minutes. Either the timeout is not firing on this path (pandoc subprocess not interruptible?) or the kill comes from somewhere else. Worth checking before assuming the timeout budget is the whole story.\n\nDeterminism evidence: two consecutive runs of the same patchset, same cell, same test — this is reproducible on the macOS lane, not a rare one-off. The contrast case remains change 1734, which contains 1731's exact commit plus one more and passed macos-latest/py3.13 both times.\n\nNo third recheck was attempted; 1731 is parked behind this bug's class fix.","timestamp":1786652175008917001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"ROOT CAUSE CONFIRMED — deterministic reproduction, and the 14-minute gap explained.\n\nMECHANISM. CI runs the unit suite with `--timeout=300 --timeout-method=thread` (.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml). pytest-timeout's *thread* method calls `os._exit(1)` from its timer thread, so the xdist worker process dies outright rather than the test failing. Reproduced locally by changing ONLY the budget:\n\n    pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py \\\n      -n 2 --dist worksteal --timeout=20 --timeout-method=thread\n\nemits `[gw0] node down: Not properly terminated` and then `worker 'gw0' crashed while running '...::test_rendered_output_is_byte_identical_to_the_landed_renderer'` — the same shape as CI, with no traceback and no assertion text.\n\nCOST. The test walks the whole committed corpus in ONE test function: 884 renderable units, each rendered twice (`_convert` plus the `_legacy_convert` oracle) = ~1768 serial pandoc spawns. Measured 91.6s idle; under saturating CPU pressure (2x hw.ncpu spinners — the fade-ea90 precedent) the SAME test measured 504.8s, i.e. 1.7x past the 300s guard. macOS is the scarcest cell in the runner pool, which is why only that cell reds.\n\nTHE 14-MINUTE GAP IS A REPORTING ARTIFACT, NOT KILL LATENCY. The two log lines are emitted by different parts of xdist at different times:\n- `node down: Not properly terminated` — xdist/workermanage.py:407, logged LIVE at the moment the worker dies.\n- `worker 'gwN' crashed while running ...` — xdist/dsession.py:436 (`handle_crashitem`), which builds an ordinary `pytest.TestReport(outcome='failed', longrepr=msg)`. Pytest prints failure reports in the FAILURES section at SESSION END, not inline.\n\nSo the elapsed time between the two lines is simply how long the surviving workers took to finish the rest of the suite — it is not evidence about how long the kill took. That fits the run arithmetic: the session totalled 1602.64s (26.7 min), the crash landed ~12.7 min in, and 14 min of suite remained. The same structure appears in my local repro, where the gap is small only because the session ended right after.\n\nBoth alternative branches are therefore not needed to explain the evidence, and neither is supported: the timeout demonstrably DOES fire on this path (the local repro kills the worker at the budget while the test is inside pandoc subprocess work), and the footprint is not an OOM candidate (the test holds ~884 short strings and spawns ONE pandoc at a time). Instrumented confirmation of both follows in the next comment.\n\nNot covered by the osprey sharing commit 48a3ba0b8a: that touched test_wiki_render_corpus.py only, and its `corpus_pass1` artifact holds pass-1 renders of whole bodies, not the per-unit `_convert`/oracle pairs this test compares. Siblings measured healthy post-48a3ba0b8a (worst call 12.5s), so this was the last test of the shape.","timestamp":1786653629163683001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"INSTRUMENTED CONFIRMATION — the 14-minute gap is a reporting artifact, and both alternative branches are refuted by measurement.\n\nEXPERIMENT. Two scratch files under a throwaway tests/unit/scratch_0078/ (removed after the run; nothing committed):\n- test_zz_gap_blocked.py — a test that parks in a blocking Popen.communicate() read on a child's pipes, i.e. exactly the shape _convert is in while pandoc runs.\n- test_aa_gap_slow.py — 24 short passing tests (5s each) that keep the session alive after the other worker dies.\nRun as: pytest tests/unit/scratch_0078 -q -n 2 --dist loadfile --timeout=20 --timeout-method=thread, with every output line timestamped relative to session start.\n\nRESULT 1 — the timeout DOES fire on this path, promptly. The test blocked inside the subprocess pipe read was killed at t+20.52s against a 20s budget. pytest-timeout's thread method runs its timer in a separate thread and calls os._exit(1), which needs no cooperation from the thread parked in the read. So 'the timeout is not firing because the pandoc subprocess is not interruptible' is refuted: it fires at the budget, to within half a second.\n\nRESULT 2 — the gap between the two log lines is remaining-session time, not kill latency. First 'node down: Not properly terminated' at t+20.52s; the \"worker 'gwN' crashed while running ...\" lines printed at t+278.48s. That is a 258-SECOND gap against a 20-SECOND budget — 12.9x — produced entirely by the surviving worker finishing its short tests. Same structure as CI's 14 minutes against 300s.\n\nThe source explains why. The two lines come from different places at different times:\n- xdist/workermanage.py:407 logs 'node down' LIVE, at the moment the worker dies.\n- xdist/dsession.py:436 (handle_crashitem) builds an ordinary pytest.TestReport(outcome='failed', longrepr=msg), and pytest prints failure reports in the FAILURES section at SESSION END.\nSo the premise 'if the per-test timeout were firing cleanly the gap should be ~5 minutes' does not hold — the gap measures how much suite remained after the crash, and carries no information about the kill. CI's arithmetic fits: session 1602.64s (26.7 min), crash ~12.7 min in, 14 min of suite left.\n\n(Incidental, and it explains why one crashing test burns so much wall clock: xdist REPLACES a crashed worker, the replacement re-runs the same poisoned test and dies too. The scratch run cycled through gw1..gw9 that way.)\n\nRESULT 3 — not OOM. Peak RSS for a process running the entire corpus comparison is 92.6 MB (/usr/bin/time -l). The macOS runner has ~7 GB and CI runs 3 workers. The test holds ~884 short strings and spawns ONE pandoc at a time, so there is no memory pressure anywhere near a kill. Refuted.\n\nCONCLUSION: single confirmed cause — the test's unbounded serial cost (91.6s idle, 504.8s saturated) crosses CI's 300s per-test guard on the contended macOS lane, and --timeout-method=thread converts that into a worker kill with no traceback rather than a test failure.\n\nFIX VERIFIED (change 1745, commit 3e8325559a).\n- Worst single case: 91.6s -> 4.37s idle; 504.8s -> 38.05s under the identical 2x hw.ncpu saturation (7.9x headroom under the 300s guard).\n- Full CI invocation 'pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -n 3 --dist worksteal --timeout=300 --timeout-method=thread': 12857 passed, 60 skipped, 0 failed, no worker crash; the test no longer appears in the slowest 8.\n- tests/integration: 194 passed, 1 skipped.\n- Coverage guard proven to fail RED: temporarily dropping a chunk made test_the_equivalence_chunks_cover_every_renderable_unit fail, then reverted.\n- All 884 units still compared, _EQUIVALENCE_STRIDE still 1, real pandoc on both sides. No timeout raise, no retry marker, no elapsed-time assertion.","timestamp":1786655574860398001}],"created_at":1786650105971258001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"37adfab1-bb91-43f3-a63b-1053c66e888c","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ce7d-3a15-51e5-4c6a"},{"link_uuid":"a3c7d5e9-cb8f-42ec-87a0-68f0b8dd8a3c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9c12-c544-4392-4ea0"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py::test_rendered_output_is_byte_identical_to_the_landed_renderer` intermittently kills its pytest-xdist worker on the macOS py3.13 `Verified` cell, reddening the whole matrix job and costing changes a `Verified -1` they did not earn (observed on change 1731 ps2; the identical commit passed in change 1734).\n\n## Root cause — CONFIRMED, reproduced deterministically\nTwo measurements, both in this worktree, name the mechanism:\n\n1. **The crash is a per-test-timeout kill, not OOM and not a pandoc fault.** CI runs the unit suite with `--timeout=300 --timeout-method=thread` (`.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml`). pytest-timeout's *thread* method calls `os._exit(1)` from its timer thread, so the xdist worker process dies outright — no traceback, no assertion text. Reproduced by lowering only the budget: `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py -n 2 --dist worksteal --timeout=20 --timeout-method=thread` emits `[gw0] node down: Not properly terminated` followed by `worker 'gw0' crashed while running '...::test_rendered_output_is_byte_identical_to_the_landed_renderer'` — byte-identical in shape to the CI report.\n2. **The test's cost is unbounded and load-dependent.** It walks the whole committed corpus in ONE test function: 884 renderable units, each rendered twice (`_convert` plus the `_legacy_convert` oracle) = ~1768 serial pandoc spawns. Measured **91.6s** idle; under saturating CPU pressure (2x `hw.ncpu` spinners, the `fade-ea90` precedent) the same test measured **504.8s** — 1.7x past the 300s guard. macOS is the scarcest cell in the runner pool, so that contention is routine, which is why only that cell reds.\n\nThe osprey cross-worker sharing commit `48a3ba0b8a` does **not** cover this file — it touched `test_wiki_render_corpus.py` only, and its `corpus_pass1` artifact holds pass-1 renders of whole bodies, not the per-unit `_convert`/oracle pairs this test compares. Siblings measured healthy post-48a3ba0b8a (worst call 12.5s), so this test is the last one of the shape.\n\n## Approach\nMake the per-test cost **bounded and independent of both load and corpus size**, without touching what is compared. Replace the single monolithic loop in `test_rendered_output_is_byte_identical_to_the_landed_renderer` with a **chunk-parametrized** test: `_renderable_units()` is computed once at module import, sliced into fixed-size batches by a new module constant `_EQUIVALENCE_CHUNK = 40`, and the test takes the chunk as a `pytest.mark.parametrize` argument keyed by chunk index.\n\nWhy this shape and not the alternatives:\n- **Fixed chunk size is the class fix.** Growing the corpus adds *cases*, never lengthens a case, so the per-test budget can never be re-crossed by fixture growth — the failure mode is closed structurally, not tuned away.\n- Every one of the 884 units is still compared against the oracle with real pandoc; `_EQUIVALENCE_STRIDE` stays 1. The byte-identity property the test exists to protect is untouched.\n- 23 cases at ~4.2s idle each leaves ~13x headroom even at the 5.5x inflation measured above, and xdist can now spread the work across workers instead of pinning it to one.\n- Explicitly NOT doing: raising `--timeout`, adding a rerun/flaky marker, or asserting on elapsed time (the wall-clock-assert gate forbids the last).\n\nA failing comparison currently reports only `assert <str> == <str>` from an anonymous loop iteration. The chunked assertion carries the unit's **global corpus index** in its message, so a future failure names which unit moved.\n\nTo keep chunking from silently dropping units, add `test_the_equivalence_chunks_cover_every_renderable_unit`: a pandoc-free test asserting the concatenation of all chunks equals `_renderable_units()` and that the total is >= 100 (the evidence floor the old inline `assert len(sampled) >= 100` provided, which moves out of the per-chunk body since no single chunk meets it).\n\nThe module docstring gains a short cost-discipline note mirroring the one `test_wiki_render_corpus.py` already carries, so the next author sees why the parametrization exists.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py` — chunk-parametrize the equivalence test, add the coverage guard, document the cost discipline. This is the only file changed; the renderer itself (`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/wiki_render.py`) is deliberately untouched, since the fault is in the test's cost profile, not in `_convert`.\n\n## Testing\nTest-only change, so the tests ARE the deliverable; verification is by measurement:\n- Happy path: the full file passes with real pandoc and every unit still compared — `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py -q --durations=0`, with no call above ~10s idle.\n- Load path (the reproduction, re-run after the fix): the same file under 2x `hw.ncpu` CPU spinners must complete with every individual call well inside 300s, where the pre-fix test measured 504.8s.\n- Failure path: the new coverage guard fails if a chunk is dropped — verified by temporarily truncating the chunk list in a scratch run and observing the guard red before reverting.\n- Regression path: the whole suite under CI's exact invocation, `pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -n 3 --dist worksteal --timeout=300 --timeout-method=thread`, must show no worker crash.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The mechanism is recorded on this ticket with its deterministic reproduction — verified by the presence of the lowered-timeout command and the 91.6s/504.8s pair above, both re-runnable in this worktree.\n- [ ] No single test in `test_wiki_render_hardening.py` exceeds ~10s idle — verified by `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py --durations=0` showing every `call` under that bound.\n- [ ] Per-test cost is bounded by construction, not by tuning — verified by reading `_EQUIVALENCE_CHUNK`: chunk size is a fixed constant, so corpus growth adds cases rather than extending any case.\n- [ ] The byte-identity property is not weakened — verified by `test_the_equivalence_chunks_cover_every_renderable_unit` asserting the chunks reassemble to exactly `_renderable_units()` (884 units, >= 100), with `_EQUIVALENCE_STRIDE` still 1 and real pandoc on both sides.\n- [ ] The fix is not a timeout raise or a retry marker — verified by the diff touching no workflow file and adding no rerun marker or elapsed-time assertion.\n- [ ] A `Verified +1` run on the change passes the macOS py3.13 cell.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py","reason":"chunk-parametrize the corpus equivalence test so per-test cost is bounded and load-independent; add a chunk-coverage guard"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","9c12-c544-4392-4ea0"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"941ca602-df75-495d-858a-6a65ba03112e","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"0078-fa3e-05d1-4e12","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Flaky CI: wiki-render hardening test kills its xdist worker on macOS","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["fef84a97-f915-4a10-a662-de95875f99e2","37adfab1-bb91-43f3-a63b-1053c66e888c","b94ccc31-1072-4789-8064-97d50f34db60","3de60824-cb2f-4ce7-9f48-2ef4805ac88d","95299c36-e67c-4d0f-a7de-729b60af90a7","941ca602-df75-495d-858a-6a65ba03112e","31d34671-f71f-4246-8658-de659cd62d33","6da15436-97de-4dec-a707-95d1251fbd71","8c2230eb-da6f-4369-aa15-3d51b015a7d3","219dd0ac-cb08-49cf-b85d-79c6052b154b","a3c7d5e9-cb8f-42ec-87a0-68f0b8dd8a3c"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786658646004708001,"uuid":"ea8cfe83-b407-4925-be46-975b9d3c5052"}